<!--
  sce:std/merge/merkle_node.scxml — one node of a merkle digest over a set
  of timestamped changes (after Actual Budget's trinary trie,
  packages/crdt/src/crdt/merkle.ts): the node at `depth` whose key is
  `prefix`, and the XOR of the hashes of every change under it.

  A change's key is its minute, `floor(millis / 60000)`, written as 30
  base-3 digits. The node at depth d (1 ≤ d ≤ 30) holds the changes whose
  minute divided by 3^(30-d) is `prefix`; the root is depth 0, prefix 0,
  and holds them all. Thirty digits are what a signed 64-bit millisecond
  clock needs and no more: the last minute it holds is 153722867280912,
  below 3^30 = 205891132094649, so the leading digit is 0, 1 or 2 for every
  wall time a hybrid logical clock (hlc_timestamp) can carry, and the digest
  is a ternary trie of one fixed depth. The reference's key is the minute
  written in base 3 as it comes, which is 16 digits only from 1997 to 3^16
  minutes (2051-11-05T13:21Z): a shorter string before, a longer one after,
  and the same minute is a different path in each.

  A clock that reads today sits under a run of nodes of prefix 0, depths 1 to
  14, each holding the whole digest: the digits of a minute below 3^16 are
  leading zeros. They are one node each however many changes the digest
  holds, and the price of a key that is the same length for every minute.

  A digest is a list of nodes in ascending (depth, prefix) — the one order
  a set of nodes has, so two digests of the same changes are equal lists
  whatever order the changes were inserted in. merkle_insert, merkle_prune
  and merkle_diff take and return it.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="merkle_node"
       sce:event-name="merge.merkle_node">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="depth" sce:type="uint8" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="prefix" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="hash" sce:type="uint32" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
